course: dictionary
lesson: 858
title: Bias: leaning towards one side
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bias means leaning towards one side instead of being fair. A referee with a bias towards one team lets that team get away with more, even when the rules say otherwise.
explain: Look for bias when you read the news, adverts or websites. Ask who wrote it, what side they want you to take, and what has been left out. «Bias means leaning towards one side; a source is where information comes from.» So always check the source.
explain: Bias can also be a verb: to bias someone is to make them one-sided. A survey that asks only your friends is biased, because it does not show what everyone thinks.
fact: Bias is an unfair way of favouring one person, side or idea over others.
fact: «Biased» means unfair and one-sided.
fact: In science and maths, bias is when the way you test or collect data pushes the results in one direction, so they are not accurate.
fact: In sewing, «on the bias» means cutting cloth diagonally across the threads.
fact: In lawn bowls, the bias is the weight that makes the ball curve.
exercise: «Videos show the exciting moments; seeing only the winners and not the losers is called survivorship bias.» What does survivorship bias mean? | *Seeing only the winners, so the picture is one-sided | Watching videos in slow motion | Seeing every moment of every game | Cheering for the losing team
exercise: Bias means leaning towards one side. What does that mean? | Falling over on purpose | Standing up straight and tall | Being fair to everyone equally | *Being unfair and favouring one side
exercise: A survey asks only your friends what they like. Why is it biased? | It was done on a Monday | It is printed in colour | *It does not show what everyone thinks | It has too many questions
test: «Remembering the times that fit your idea and forgetting the times that don't is called confirmation bias.» What is this kind of bias called? | Survivorship bias | *Confirmation bias | Sewing bias | Fair testing
test: Which word means unfair and one-sided? | *Biased | Balanced | Equal | Careful
exam: A referee with a bias towards one team is most likely to do what? | *Make unfair decisions that help that team | Give both teams exactly the same chances | Ask the crowd to vote on every call | Stop the game and go home
